WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:07.700 align:start position:0%
If you lay your egg on the ice at -40°
it freezes solid in minutes. So you sit

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:11.000 align:start position:0%
on it like a chicken,
like [clears throat] a penguin. But the

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:15.100 align:start position:0%
ice still touches the egg from below and
freezes it from underneath. So you lift

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:19.600 align:start position:0%
it onto your feet and cover it with a
warm flap of belly skin like a sleeping

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:23.700 align:start position:0%
bag. But mom starved for weeks to make
that egg and she has to go back to the

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:28.500 align:start position:0%
sea to eat. So you roll the egg over to
dad, feet to feet super fast before it

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:33.600 align:start position:0%
freezes. But now dad has to stand in a
freezing storm for two whole months

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:37.800 align:start position:0%
without eating a single bite. So
thousands of dads squeeze together in a

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:41.600 align:start position:0%
giant huddle, warm like a hot tub in the
middle and take turns on the cold edge.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:45.900 align:start position:0%
But the chick hatches before mom gets
back and there's no food anywhere. So

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:50.100 align:start position:0%
you make a special milk inside your
throat and burp it up to feed your baby.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.600 align:start position:0%
Congratulations. You built a healthy
penguin.

